=begin pod

=head1 NAME

L10N::ES - Spanish localization of Raku

=head1 SYNOPSIS

=begin output
$ spaku -e 'dí "Hola Mundo"'
Hola Mundo
=end output

=begin code :lang<raku>
# Must have RAKUDO_RAKUAST=1 environment variable set
# when running a Rakudo older than the 2026.09 release
use L10N::ES;
dí "Hola Mundo";
=end code

=head1 DESCRIPTION

The C<L10N::ES> distribution contains the logic to provide a Spanish
localization of the Raku Programming Language.  It installs a
C<spaku> executable that will automatically activate the Spanish
localization.  And it allows one to use the Spanish localization
in selected programs with a C<use L10N::ES> statement.

=head1 AUTHORS

Elizabeth Mattijsen, Ignacio Martinoli

